  "visualBrief": "Individual medium-fi Hagia Sophia in Thessaloniki: ochre west upper facade and exposed warm masonry lower/east walls, three west doors with a broad round central portal, four lower arched window fields and a narrow upper clerestory row. Square brick drum with large arched glazing, short round crown and low ribbed gray-green metal dome/cross. Low red tiled main roof, large polygonal eastern apse with smaller side apses, and northwest small bell tower/open paired arches and hip cap. Retained mapped plans and terrain-following footings. Separate unmapped courtyard gateway/retaining wall/fence, surrounding town/landscaping, exact carved reliefs/icons/text, interiors and certified walking excluded.",
